Begin and end with $1$. Add adjacent entries of Row $6$ to obtain the interior entries.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=11mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\node[anchor=east] at (-4.3,0) {Row $6$};
\node[anchor=east] at (-4.3,-1) {Row $7$};
\foreach \pos/\val in {-3/1,-2/6,-1/15,0/20,1/15,2/6,3/1} {\node at (\pos,0) {$\val$};}
\foreach \pos/\val in {-3.5/1,-2.5/7,-1.5/21,-0.5/35,0.5/35,1.5/21,2.5/7,3.5/1} {\node at (\pos,-1) {$\val$};}
\draw[black,->] (-0.9,-0.22) -- (-0.6,-0.75);
\draw[black,->] (-0.1,-0.22) -- (-0.4,-0.75);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For example, $15+20=35$. Row $7$ is $1,7,21,35,35,21,7,1$.
